// The wyhash module (devices/wyhash.ent), written in ent-lang on the
// built-in `mul_wide`: its values are those of wyhash.h (final version
// 4.2), whose `wyrand` from the state 42 gives the three numbers below one
// after another.
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/wyhash_use.ent | FileCheck %s
// Drawn from the key and the number alone: the same on all cores.
// RUN: %ent run --parallel %S/Inputs/wyhash_use.ent | FileCheck %s

// CHECK:      mul_wide 81621149086635842 2465395958572223728
// CHECK-NEXT: wymix 2528527714576915378
// CHECK-NEXT: wyhash64 5942532942210584115 18027973888215709232
// CHECK-NEXT: wyrand 14587678697106979209 9105053682160394182 14839644324764355487
// CHECK-NEXT: unit 0.493586 below 3
// CHECK-NEXT: faces 2466
// CHECK-NOT:  {{.}}
